# Everything here is DELETED from $HOME on every host that applies, and
# bin/chezmoi-update fans out to five accounts across three machines.
#
# The editor-backup globs below are deliberately enumerated per directory rather
# than written as `**/*~`. A recursive glob here would match every ~-suffixed
# file anywhere under $HOME -- including ~/Documents, ~/Code and ~/Nextcloud --
# and delete them on all five accounts. Keep these bounded to directories
# chezmoi actually manages. (.chezmoiignore is a different story: it is
# non-destructive, so `**/*~` is correct there.)
*~
.bashrc.d/*~
.config/*~
.config/*/*~
bin/*~
DEADJOE
.config/fish/themes/Catppuccin Mocha.theme
.config/fish/themes/Catppuccin Macchiato.theme
.config/ghostty/config.ghostty
.bashrc.d/chezmoi-completion.sh
.config/neofetch
.config/hyfetch.json
